cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its research package, please cite it as below."
title: "Onyx: a local-model code editor with a simulated, measured agent harness"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lloyd
    given-names: Sheehan
repository-code: "https://github.com/sheehanlloyd/Onyx"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0-alpha.1
date-released: 2026-11-22
abstract: >-
  A fork of Code - OSS that runs coding models on the user's machine and treats the model as an
  untrusted, measurable component. The repository includes a written harness contract with
  fourteen invariants, a deterministic simulation rig that checks them, a mutation corpus of
  the project's own fixed defects, ten pre-registered hypotheses with their outcomes (four
  supported, one refuted, five inconclusive), the raw results, and one command per published
  number. The version and date above describe the research package in the repository; no
  binary release had been published on that date.
keywords:
  - local language models
  - code editor
  - agent harness
  - simulation testing
  - mutation testing
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Code - OSS (Visual Studio Code open-source project)"
    authors:
      - name: "Microsoft Corporation"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/microsoft/vscode"
    license: MIT
